cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite both the software and the associated manuscript."
title: "Analysis code for: Nutrition–inflammation gene-expression axes associate with myeloid inflammatory activity but do not predict survival in non-small cell lung cancer: a TCGA transcriptomic analysis"
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-18
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23427752"          # concept DOI (all versions); the v1.0.0 version DOI is 10.5281/zenodo.23427753
url: "https://github.com/ximeng007cmx/nsclc_nutrition_inflammation"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ximeng007cmx/nsclc_nutrition_inflammation"
abstract: >-
  Analysis pipeline for a TCGA pan-cancer RNA-seq study of three a-priori
  nutrition-inflammation gene-expression axes (16 genes each) in non-small cell
  lung cancer. The pipeline performs stream subsetting of the UCSC Xena Toil
  RSEM FPKM compendium, reversal of the stored log2(FPKM + 0.001) encoding,
  Ensembl-to-symbol collapse, ssGSEA scoring, LASSO-Cox modelling in the
  TCGA-LUAD training cohort, internal hold-out validation with repeated 7:3
  splits, cross-histology generalisation to TCGA-LUSC, three pre-specified
  sensitivity analyses (endpoint, feature scheme, training direction), two
  robustness modules (random expression-matched null panels and Spearman
  partial correlations controlling for the ESTIMATE tumour-purity estimate),
  and analysis of the tumour immune microenvironment using pathway-level
  activity proxies from real MSigDB C5 GO:BP and HALLMARK entries. The axes
  associate with myeloid inflammatory activity but do not predict survival
  (internal hold-out C-index 0.494; median repeated-split C-index 0.542); the
  prognostic result is reported as an honest negative. All scripts are shipped
  unmodified except for one hard-coded project root, which relocate.py rewrites
  on the user's machine.
keywords:
  - non-small cell lung cancer
  - advanced lung cancer inflammation index
  - nutritional status
  - tumour immune microenvironment
  - myeloid inflammation
  - transcriptomic signature
  - ssGSEA
  - LASSO-Cox
  - TCGA
  - reproducibility
